<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS - AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$48 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS - AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$48 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two promissory note issuers came to the market for a total of A$48 million on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Australian state-owned telecommunications group Telstra Corp sold A$20 million of one-month paper at a touch over the mid-rate for the corresponding bank bill.</p>
<p>The physical bank bill yield curve has moved lower in sympathy with overnight weakness in the U.S. debt market.</p>
<p>At 2345 GMT (11.45 a.m.), December bank bill futures were trading four points lower at 92.73.</p>
